course: dictionary
lesson: 15351
title: Solidified
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Solidified has two meanings, and the context tells you which one to use. If something was runny and then went hard, it means it turned from a liquid into a solid.
explain: «The lava flowed down the hill, then solidified into black rock.» Lava is hot liquid rock, and rock is solid, so solidified means it cooled and became solid.
explain: «Their friendship solidified after the school trip.» A friendship cannot turn into rock, so the word must mean something else: it became stronger and more certain. Test it by swapping in "became firmer", and the sentence still makes sense.
fact: Solidified means turned from a liquid or gas into a solid, often by cooling.
fact: Solidified also means made stronger, firmer or more certain.
fact: Water solidifies into ice at 0°C.
fact: «The melted chocolate solidified in the fridge.» The liquid chocolate became solid as it cooled.
fact: Solidify is the verb. Its other forms are solidifies, solidifying and solidified.
exercise: «The wax solidified on the table.» What does solidified mean here? | Melted into a puddle | *Turned from liquid into solid as it cooled | Blew away in the wind | Made stronger and firmer
exercise: «Their team's plan solidified after a long talk.» What does solidified mean here? | *Became firmer and more certain | Turned into ice | Got lost | Melted away
exercise: Which change is solidifying? | Steam rising from a kettle | Ice cream dripping down a cone | Ice melting into water | *Water freezing into ice
test: What is the opposite of solidifying, as in «lava solidified into rock»? | *Melting | Cooking | Freezing | Hardening
test: «Their friendship solidified over the year.» Which meaning fits? | Turned into liquid | Dissolved in water | Became weaker and wobbly | *Became stronger and more certain
exam: «The hot glue solidified quickly on the paper.» What does solidified mean? | Melted into a puddle | Dissolved and vanished | Became stronger and firmer | *Turned from liquid into solid as it cooled
